<form id="skill-form" class="skill-form" autocomplete="off" novalidate>
    <div id="skill-title" class="skill-title"></div>
    <div class="skill-row skill-row-top">
        <input id="skill-name" class="skill-field skill-name" type="text" placeholder="name" spellcheck="false" />
        <div id="skill-dependencies" class="multiselect">
            <button type="button" class="multiselect-toggle" aria-haspopup="listbox" aria-expanded="false">
                <span class="multiselect-label">MultiSelect &lt;Dependencies&gt;</span>
            </button>
            <div class="multiselect-menu">
                <input class="multiselect-search" type="search" placeholder="filter skills" spellcheck="false" aria-label="filter skills" />
                <div class="multiselect-options" role="listbox" aria-multiselectable="true"></div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <button type="button" id="skill-new" class="skill-square" title="new skill depending on this one" aria-label="new skill depending on this one">+</button>
    </div>
    <div class="skill-row">
        <input id="skill-description" class="skill-field" type="text" placeholder="description" spellcheck="false" />
        <input id="skill-url" class="skill-field" type="text" placeholder="url" spellcheck="false" />
    </div>
    <div class="skill-row">
        <input id="skill-keywords" class="skill-field" type="text" placeholder="keywords (space separated, searchable)" spellcheck="false" />
    </div>
    <textarea id="skill-content" class="skill-content" spellcheck="false" placeholder="# &lt;skill-name&gt;

&lt;One sentence: what this skill lets an agent do.&gt;

## when to load

- &lt;trigger phrase a user would actually type&gt;
- &lt;trigger phrase&gt;
- &lt;trigger phrase&gt;

## dependencies

- `&lt;project&gt;/&lt;skill-name&gt;` — owns &lt;ground&gt;. This skill assumes it and does not re-teach it.
  `get-skill(project: &quot;&lt;project&gt;&quot;, name: &quot;&lt;skill-name&gt;&quot;)`
- none — this skill stands alone.

## procedure

1. **&lt;verb-first step&gt;** — &lt;what to do, and why it matters&gt;.
2. **&lt;verb-first step&gt;** — &lt;what to do&gt;.
3. **&lt;verb-first step&gt;** — &lt;what to do&gt;.

## checklist — done when

- [ ] &lt;observable result the reader can verify&gt;
- [ ] &lt;observable result&gt;
- [ ] &lt;observable result&gt;
"></textarea>
    <div class="skill-row skill-actions">
        <span class="skill-status" role="status"></span>
        <button type="button" id="skill-revert" class="skill-button">Revert</button>
        <button type="submit" id="skill-save" class="skill-button skill-save">Save</button>
    </div>
</form>
